# Secrets and providers

- Keep keys in untracked `.env` files or secret storage. `.env.example` may contain only empty or local-safe values.
- Mobile builds may contain public API base URLs only.
- Do not send names, voice samples, precise location, contacts, or other child PII to AI providers.
- Do not call OpenRouter, ElevenLabs, or object-storage credentials from the client.
- Rotate any credential that appears in source, logs, screenshots, issues, or MCP configuration.
- MCP is development tooling, not a runtime dependency. Do not give MCP production database or provider credentials.
